WEBVTT

00:00:11.110 --> 00:00:15.640
My right hand holds a bowl of gold,

00:00:15.640 --> 00:00:20.180
And my left holds one of silver.

00:00:20.180 --> 00:00:24.720
Never one without the other,

00:00:24.720 --> 00:00:37.800
Two unseen bowls for each of us.

00:00:37.800 --> 00:00:46.210
The golden one is filled with joy,

00:00:46.210 --> 00:00:53.550
shining warmly.

00:00:53.550 --> 00:00:58.350
Since we met, my golden bowl

00:00:58.350 --> 00:01:05.360
cannot hold all my happiness and love.

00:01:07.100 --> 00:01:15.500
Golden joy, silver sadness,

00:01:15.500 --> 00:01:22.850
I would leave my past behind...

00:01:22.850 --> 00:01:27.580
For you, for the sake of love,

00:01:27.580 --> 00:01:34.520
I would empty the bowls of my past.

00:02:07.250 --> 00:02:09.400
What is this about?

00:02:12.150 --> 00:02:13.290
You know already.

00:02:14.170 --> 00:02:14.910
Yes.

00:02:15.960 --> 00:02:20.450
This is the elm tree where Rei waited for you yesterday!

00:02:21.090 --> 00:02:23.500
She got soaked and caught a fever!

00:02:24.890 --> 00:02:28.240
Don't you care at all what happens to Rei? ?

00:02:28.910 --> 00:02:31.250
It is of no concern to me.

00:02:32.230 --> 00:02:33.100
But Rei...

00:02:33.870 --> 00:02:35.610
But Rei is your younger sister!

00:02:48.170 --> 00:02:51.920
<b>13. A Tale of Double Suicide</b>

00:02:57.850 --> 00:02:58.730
Who's there?

00:03:04.140 --> 00:03:05.010
Wait, please.

00:03:06.240 --> 00:03:07.520
I haven't finished!

00:03:09.210 --> 00:03:12.150
I don't need to waste my time listening to this.

00:03:12.990 --> 00:03:13.260
Rei... <b> </b>

00:03:13.260 --> 00:03:15.070
Rei... Did Rei send you here?

00:03:16.700 --> 00:03:20.380
I'm certain she would never ask you to speak to me.

00:03:21.220 --> 00:03:23.630
Regardless... you're an outsider, and must stay out of this.

00:03:24.260 --> 00:03:27.680
Despite your friendship. And despite your feelings.

00:03:31.370 --> 00:03:32.240
Good day.

00:03:39.670 --> 00:03:40.680
Her sister...?

00:03:41.260 --> 00:03:43.270
Saint-Juste is Miya-sama's sister...?

00:03:43.710 --> 00:03:46.190
No way... Can it be true?

00:03:48.810 --> 00:03:49.680
Oh, my Brother...

00:03:53.320 --> 00:03:58.080
Chigusa-Cho... 1-17-15 Maison d'Eduard.

00:03:58.190 --> 00:03:59.260
Room 507.

00:04:00.270 --> 00:04:02.280
An icy room filled with mirrors...

00:04:03.470 --> 00:04:05.420
...a light in the kitchen that doesn't work...

00:04:06.470 --> 00:04:11.900
...that's Saint-Juste's... that's her room...

00:04:11.900 --> 00:04:15.450
That's her lonely room... her lonely little world.

00:04:20.690 --> 00:04:23.970
My dear Brother... the sandwich I left for her...

00:04:24.060 --> 00:04:28.020
That sandwich remains untouched at her door.

00:05:11.090 --> 00:05:14.100
So... are you in your room right now? Or out?

00:05:15.170 --> 00:05:17.510
My phone calls are all that can penetrate your world.

00:05:18.910 --> 00:05:21.450
I can't enter your world myself.

00:05:23.270 --> 00:05:27.620
I can only hope that you will open your door of your own free will...

00:05:28.020 --> 00:05:31.100
...smiling, and saying "Hi"...

00:05:31.550 --> 00:05:34.630
...emerging from your deep, dark, mysterious world.

00:05:34.630 --> 00:05:36.370
From your private world.

00:05:37.860 --> 00:05:40.880
I heard today that you are Miya-sama's sister.

00:05:42.670 --> 00:05:45.420
The two of you have different last names.

00:05:45.690 --> 00:05:48.770
How could this be? And what does it mean?

00:05:49.580 --> 00:05:55.540
But, those things aside, are you eating well?

00:05:55.780 --> 00:05:57.260
What about your fever?

00:05:58.760 --> 00:06:00.570
I worry about you...

00:06:33.250 --> 00:06:33.990
But Rei...

00:06:35.070 --> 00:06:36.880
But Rei is your younger sister!

00:07:06.580 --> 00:07:08.120
I've been looking for you all over, Rei!

00:07:08.850 --> 00:07:11.060
What on earth are you doing out with a fever like that!

00:07:11.730 --> 00:07:12.670
Leave me alone.

00:07:13.300 --> 00:07:14.580
Let's go home.

00:07:14.710 --> 00:07:16.050
You have to rest.

00:07:25.130 --> 00:07:27.880
Tell me... please... did you visit the elm tree?

00:07:28.630 --> 00:07:29.300
Yes.

00:07:29.740 --> 00:07:32.020
She was waiting for me, right?

00:07:34.330 --> 00:07:35.070
Mmm...

00:07:35.730 --> 00:07:38.010
Did you tell her why I wasn't there?

00:07:38.610 --> 00:07:40.020
Did you explain it all?

00:07:41.980 --> 00:07:43.120
Stop your nonsense.

00:07:43.690 --> 00:07:45.100
Why won't you be reasonable!

00:08:15.730 --> 00:08:18.750
Umm... hello? Yes, Asaka....

00:08:19.120 --> 00:08:20.930
Sai... Saint-Juste-sama!

00:08:21.280 --> 00:08:25.370
How are you? How do you feel? Did you eat something?

00:08:25.440 --> 00:08:26.440
Some soup.

00:08:27.250 --> 00:08:29.260
I'm fixing some for her.

00:08:29.680 --> 00:08:30.750
Kaoru-no-Kimi!

00:08:31.700 --> 00:08:34.990
Oh, thank goodness! You're there with her!

00:08:35.390 --> 00:08:39.410
I'm so relieved! Saint-Juste isn't alone...!

00:08:39.530 --> 00:08:41.540
She's sleeping right now.

00:08:42.010 --> 00:08:44.900
She's still got a bit of fever, but it's nothing to worry about.

00:08:45.390 --> 00:08:47.200
I'm coming over now!

00:08:47.820 --> 00:08:49.830
Don't you know what time it is?

00:08:50.070 --> 00:08:53.420
It's well past the time for freshmen to be out.

00:08:53.790 --> 00:08:57.400
I'll get to the convenience store... and brings lots of good food...

00:08:57.670 --> 00:08:59.350
No, don't. I'll hang up now.

00:08:59.640 --> 00:09:03.390
Um... what kind of food... does Saint-Juste like?

00:09:03.850 --> 00:09:06.190
Huh? Who knows...

00:09:06.920 --> 00:09:11.810
Come to think of it... I don't remember ever seeing her enjoy eating...

00:09:14.770 --> 00:09:15.840
Anyway, I'm coming!

00:09:29.670 --> 00:09:31.410
I'd like to take a shower.

00:09:32.320 --> 00:09:34.940
I won't allow it. Not with your fever.

00:09:49.770 --> 00:09:51.040
Rei, what's the matter?

00:10:05.770 --> 00:10:06.440
Rei!

00:10:08.680 --> 00:10:09.350
Rei!

00:10:34.920 --> 00:10:36.120
If I could only wash it off...

00:10:38.360 --> 00:10:39.770
...I want to wash all of it off!

00:11:01.770 --> 00:11:02.510
I'm cold.

00:11:03.460 --> 00:11:04.400
No wonder.

00:11:31.980 --> 00:11:33.190
Here... here it is.

00:11:33.780 --> 00:11:36.060
How about coffee? I'll make some.

00:11:40.790 --> 00:11:43.800
Before you do that, maybe you should help me get her dressed.

00:12:09.110 --> 00:12:15.600
Saint-Juste remained asleep the entire time I was there in her room with her.

00:12:20.610 --> 00:12:22.220
This is fine here.

00:12:22.490 --> 00:12:25.700
I'll catch a cab at the main street.

00:12:26.310 --> 00:12:27.380
Are you sure you'll be OK?

00:12:27.580 --> 00:12:30.000
You shouldn't go to school after getting no sleep all night.

00:12:30.240 --> 00:12:33.050
I'll be fine. I'm good at handling hardships.

00:12:39.390 --> 00:12:40.460
We can only wait for her...

00:12:40.760 --> 00:12:41.500
Huh?

00:12:41.760 --> 00:12:44.040
When she finally gives up fighting this thing alone,

00:12:44.480 --> 00:12:47.900
...that's when she'll come to us for help.

00:12:48.410 --> 00:12:49.890
So that she can get over it.

00:12:50.020 --> 00:12:54.170
So that she can finally get over this agony and start to live again.

00:12:54.850 --> 00:13:01.760
Waiting this out is a test of my friendship.

00:13:05.390 --> 00:13:08.880
But she can be very trying...

00:13:11.200 --> 00:13:12.540
Take care.

00:13:12.930 --> 00:13:13.740
Thanks.

00:13:17.790 --> 00:13:18.800
My Dear Brother...

00:13:20.000 --> 00:13:24.830
This thing which connects them both so closely...

00:13:25.500 --> 00:13:28.310
...is this what true friendship is?

00:13:29.420 --> 00:13:35.050
If that is how real friendship works, it's so different from me and Tomoko.

00:13:35.830 --> 00:13:38.780
We are much more selfish about our friendship.

00:13:39.110 --> 00:13:42.330
We think of friendship as something which entitles,

00:13:42.330 --> 00:13:44.740
...not as something which obligates.

00:13:45.830 --> 00:13:48.710
They are only a year older than us...

00:13:48.710 --> 00:13:54.610
...yet they are so much more kind to each other, so much more patient.

00:13:54.610 --> 00:13:56.750
It's hard to understand why and how that could be.

00:13:56.940 --> 00:14:02.430
Unless it is something more special than mere friendship.

00:14:02.630 --> 00:14:08.930
Unless this is a deeper bond based on some kind of doomed emotion...

00:14:12.970 --> 00:14:17.450
Ah... the sun is shining, everything is lush and green!

00:14:17.670 --> 00:14:21.950
This is a heaven of dancing birds, glistening water, and singing flowers...

00:14:21.960 --> 00:14:23.630
...all telling me to be happy!

00:14:23.780 --> 00:14:27.060
But despite all this loveliness, a doom awaits us.

00:14:27.260 --> 00:14:30.880
A terrible doom! Also known as "mid-terms"...

00:14:31.940 --> 00:14:33.020
Tomoko-san!

00:14:33.020 --> 00:14:36.030
You should eat something before afternoon classes start!

00:14:36.410 --> 00:14:40.830
No thanks... I'm too depressed to have an appetite.

00:14:41.290 --> 00:14:42.290
...but-but-but!

00:14:43.760 --> 00:14:46.110
But eating is my way of fighting back!

00:14:46.110 --> 00:14:48.450
Anyway, it helps me keep a positive attitude.

00:14:50.650 --> 00:14:53.600
I envy all you sorority members!

00:14:53.600 --> 00:14:56.350
You guys are different from us... you look so confident.

00:14:56.440 --> 00:14:58.860
Hey, I'm not confident!

00:14:59.320 --> 00:15:01.270
I know about your cram sessions.

00:15:01.470 --> 00:15:05.020
Your sorority sisters are telling you what's covered on the tests!

00:15:05.160 --> 00:15:07.770
Yes, but not ALL that's covered.

00:15:07.850 --> 00:15:10.270
Please, Nanako, you're my friend!

00:15:10.330 --> 00:15:11.810
Now you can prove your friendship! <b> </b>

00:15:11.810 --> 00:15:12.610
Now you can prove your friendship!

00:15:12.810 --> 00:15:16.770
Loan me your cram school notes! I'll make a copy and return them!

00:15:18.220 --> 00:15:20.570
Oh! Please? Mariko, you too, please ?

00:15:55.450 --> 00:15:58.530
It was early afternoon after lunch...

00:15:58.530 --> 00:16:01.280
...that was when the strange rumors began.

00:16:05.950 --> 00:16:10.040
The first one was that piano music was heard in the music hall...

00:16:10.040 --> 00:16:12.250
...but there was no one inside.

00:16:12.870 --> 00:16:15.890
Another one was that during 4th period,

00:16:15.890 --> 00:16:17.900
...footsteps were heard in the empty north building,

00:16:17.900 --> 00:16:21.450
...going up and down, up and down the stairs.

00:16:21.580 --> 00:16:22.650
Did you hear it? <b> </b>

00:16:22.660 --> 00:16:22.920
Did you hear it? Wow, that's scary!

00:16:22.920 --> 00:16:23.730
Did you hear it?

00:16:23.730 --> 00:16:24.130
Is it true? Did you hear it?

00:16:24.130 --> 00:16:25.270
Is it true? <b> </b>

00:16:25.950 --> 00:16:27.760
Then there was the third rumor.

00:16:27.760 --> 00:16:30.240
It gave me a bit of a chill.

00:16:30.780 --> 00:16:33.390
That there was a sound from the elm tree,

00:16:33.390 --> 00:16:38.010
...a deep, soulful, sad sobbing... ...carried aloft by the wind,

00:16:38.010 --> 00:16:41.560
...which was heard from as far away as the library.

00:16:42.010 --> 00:16:46.760
Those substances which oxidize other materials are called oxidants.

00:16:46.760 --> 00:16:52.390
While oxidizing other materials, oxidants themselves are reduced during the process.

00:16:54.390 --> 00:16:55.190
What?

00:16:55.330 --> 00:16:57.610
Nanako-san, you're so naive!

00:16:58.550 --> 00:17:02.570
We always hear these sorts of rumors just before exams.

00:17:03.210 --> 00:17:04.810
Before exams?

00:17:05.040 --> 00:17:07.660
Yes... everyone gets so terribly stressed and nervous!

00:17:08.180 --> 00:17:11.930
So they start mixing up fact and fiction like that...

00:17:12.930 --> 00:17:15.080
Mmmm... I get it.

00:17:15.490 --> 00:17:18.570
Perhaps you could say it is a tradition here at Seiran...

00:17:19.290 --> 00:17:21.840
The rumors before last year's exams were even scarier!

00:17:22.670 --> 00:17:27.970
The story is that someone was seen at the piano in the music hall.

00:17:28.640 --> 00:17:32.530
The scary thing was that there were actually two of them...

00:17:33.700 --> 00:17:37.110
One was a splendid woman in men's attire, a white tuxedo;

00:17:37.280 --> 00:17:39.760
The other was a female student in a hakama.

00:17:41.150 --> 00:17:44.030
Every afternoon they were seen,

00:17:44.030 --> 00:17:48.120
...climbing the stairs of the north building, up and down,

00:17:48.120 --> 00:17:50.870
...in the fading light of the sunset.

00:17:51.500 --> 00:17:57.270
They were said to be Seiran seniors from the beginning of the <i>Showa</i> era.

00:17:57.570 --> 00:17:59.650
And they were doomed lovers.

00:18:05.320 --> 00:18:09.140
Finally, they cut their wrists with a razor,

00:18:10.610 --> 00:18:13.220
...together, under the elm tree, in the rain...

00:18:16.320 --> 00:18:20.470
Somehow, those two always reappear at exam time!

00:18:21.810 --> 00:18:24.080
Actually, I think it's a deliciously romantic story...

00:18:24.390 --> 00:18:28.750
Hmmm... that elm tree, in the courtyard... it has such a history...!

00:18:29.960 --> 00:18:30.830
Why? What?

00:18:31.520 --> 00:18:33.860
Why did they have to die?

00:18:34.480 --> 00:18:35.550
I don't know.

00:18:37.230 --> 00:18:39.040
But it must have made them happy...

00:18:39.930 --> 00:18:41.810
...being able to die with someone they loved...

00:18:45.670 --> 00:18:48.420
Wait. Hey! Are you implying something...?

00:18:48.820 --> 00:18:51.300
Well, Nanako-san, let's go to the sorority house!

00:18:51.790 --> 00:18:53.600
Our cram session is about to start.

00:18:55.170 --> 00:18:58.120
Well, off I go. See you tomorrow, Tomoko-san!

00:18:58.550 --> 00:19:00.770
Ah... um... oh!

00:19:00.770 --> 00:19:03.180
Good luck! Don't forget the notes!

00:19:03.550 --> 00:19:05.090
Nanako, what's the matter?

00:19:05.940 --> 00:19:07.420
Eh? Nothing...

00:19:08.050 --> 00:19:09.190
You were up all night. <b> </b>

00:19:09.190 --> 00:19:09.920
You were up all night. What ?

00:19:11.210 --> 00:19:12.280
That's OK, I guess.

00:19:12.430 --> 00:19:15.110
Well! Study hard, then, at your cram session.

00:19:15.450 --> 00:19:16.460
Bye!

00:19:18.080 --> 00:19:19.690
Bye, Tomoko!

00:19:21.270 --> 00:19:22.410
Oh, Tomoko...

00:19:35.520 --> 00:19:36.660
It's coming from the music hall...

00:19:43.900 --> 00:19:45.240
Is something wrong?

00:19:45.550 --> 00:19:47.960
Go on ahead to the sorority house, everyone.

00:19:49.350 --> 00:19:51.160
I'll be there shortly.

00:19:56.050 --> 00:19:58.190
I'm sure of it! That melody...!

00:20:52.800 --> 00:20:54.140
Saint-Juste-sama...!

00:21:01.460 --> 00:21:02.740
Hello.

00:21:03.890 --> 00:21:04.890
Hello.

00:21:05.380 --> 00:21:06.990
So you came here.

00:21:07.560 --> 00:21:08.630
Are you well?

00:21:09.530 --> 00:21:11.470
I waited. Forever.

00:21:12.030 --> 00:21:12.840
Forever!

00:21:13.100 --> 00:21:14.510
Under that elm tree.

00:21:15.090 --> 00:21:17.030
I heard you've had a fever.

00:21:18.050 --> 00:21:19.120
That's not good.

00:21:26.150 --> 00:21:29.300
Very bad. Your fever is still high.

00:21:34.860 --> 00:21:37.410
I'd like you to go home. To your room.

00:21:37.630 --> 00:21:38.910
Rest yourself there.

00:21:41.240 --> 00:21:42.310
All right.

00:22:00.660 --> 00:22:01.790
Saint-Juste-sama!

00:22:04.280 --> 00:22:05.550
Saint-Juste-sama!

00:22:21.180 --> 00:22:22.660
Saint-Juste-sama!

00:22:24.410 --> 00:22:26.280
SAINT-JUSTE-SAMA...!

00:22:44.430 --> 00:22:47.580
Be here! Saint-Juste-sama, you have to be here!

00:22:59.620 --> 00:23:00.890
Saint-Juste-sama! <b> </b>

00:23:00.890 --> 00:23:01.900
Saint-Juste-sama! Fukiko-sama!

00:23:12.140 --> 00:23:13.480
I've been waiting...!

00:23:13.830 --> 00:23:15.440
All this time... all this time...

00:23:16.030 --> 00:23:18.570
I knew you would someday keep your promise to me!

00:23:19.670 --> 00:23:20.880
Fukiko-sama!

00:23:22.690 --> 00:23:24.500
No! I'm not her!

00:23:24.880 --> 00:23:27.560
It's just as you told me then...

00:23:28.500 --> 00:23:31.380
...you've come here so we can... die together...

00:23:32.850 --> 00:23:34.250
Saint-Juste-sama!

00:23:34.850 --> 00:23:36.720
...you said... we could die together...

00:23:39.860 --> 00:23:42.810
She's mad! She's gone completely mad!

00:23:44.560 --> 00:23:45.570
Brother...!

00:24:10.160 --> 00:24:14.360
I dreamed I was chasing a rainbow...

00:24:14.360 --> 00:24:19.830
Then the rainbow I was chasing was you.

00:24:21.300 --> 00:24:25.440
Before, I had no strength, no will.

00:24:25.440 --> 00:24:30.910
But now because of you, I do.

00:24:31.650 --> 00:24:37.190
Feelings of love, like raindrops

00:24:37.190 --> 00:24:42.660
Come pouring from the sky.

00:24:42.660 --> 00:24:45.390
This is surely a game

00:24:45.390 --> 00:24:48.200
Of some mischievous fairy...

00:24:48.200 --> 00:24:50.600
Always dancing,

00:24:50.600 --> 00:24:55.870
Always capricious...

00:25:01.550 --> 00:25:03.630
Preview

00:25:03.960 --> 00:25:07.440
Rei embraces Nanako, insisting that they die together.

00:25:08.040 --> 00:25:11.320
Though she struggles to escape from the deranged Rei...

00:25:11.320 --> 00:25:14.340
...Nanako ends up cornered against the wall.

00:25:15.190 --> 00:25:16.600
Rei draws her knife...

00:25:16.950 --> 00:25:19.760
What is the madness which flashes in her eyes?

00:25:20.310 --> 00:25:21.380
Next episode: <b> </b>

00:25:21.380 --> 00:25:23.320
Next episode: <b>The Secret Door</b>

00:25:23.520 --> 00:25:25.060
Brother, Dear Brother... <b> </b>

00:25:25.070 --> 00:25:28.210
Brother, Dear Brother... There is no end to my tears...
